  "position": "Mechanical recompute of all five preregistered instrument-validity criteria directly from the 20 raw records in data/trials/exp010_v21_pilot.jsonl, by my own stdlib-only script, with no import of, call to, or read of falsify/analyze.py and without running bin/falsify analyze: V1 PASS (20/20), V2 PASS (20/20), V3a PASS (83 reserve events), V3b PASS (77/83 = 0.927710843373494), V3c PASS (77), V4 PASS (20/20), V5 PASS on its invalid-trials limb (0/20). OVERALL VERDICT: PASS. No criterion is marginal - every margin is at or near ceiling. Reserve counts are high, so the low-reserve FAIL path is not triggered and there is nothing to recharacterize. Confidence high on V1-V4, where I recomputed reserve events and their both_paths_open flags myself from the per-action env_events log and found 20/20 trial-level agreement with the measured aggregates (zero disagreements). Confidence qualified on V5: its parse_failures conjunct is not logged anywhere in the trial file and is therefore unevaluable from the preregistered artifact; I scored V5 PASS on the computable invalid-trials limb and state the parse limb as unmeasurable rather than silently assuming zero. Instrument validation only - no hypothesis verdict, no decision recommendation.",
  "provenance": "RECOVERED_FROM_CHECKPOINT: runner died before self-submitting; numbers are its own on-disk product. Independence audited by lead (stdlib only; reads only raw JSONL + spec threshold; no reference to falsify/analyze.py or any lead artifact).",
  "provenance_note_by_author": "Runner died after my script wrote partial.json and tmp_independent_analyst.json. The lead reconstructed a reduced tmp file from my partial.json; this version restores the full detail from that same checkpoint, which is my own on-disk product. Numbers are byte-identical to the checkpoint and the script reruns reproducibly.",
  "role": "independent analyst - from-scratch second computation of the V1-V5 instrument validity bar for exp010_v21_pilot",
